There are n petrol pumps along a circular route, where the amount of petrol at the ith station is petrol[I]. 
You have a car with an unlimited petrol tank and it costs cost[i] of petrol to travel from the ith station to its 
next (i + 1)th station.
You begin the journey with an empty tank at one of the petrol stations. Given two integer arrays petrol and cost,
 return the starting
 petrol station's index if you can travel around the circuit once in the clockwise direction, otherwise return -1
 . If there exists a solution, 
 it is guaranteed to be unique.
